  "note": "Informational mapping from PyPI Trove 'License ::' classifiers (as published at pypi.org/classifiers, via the trove-classifiers project) to SPDX license ids, not legal advice. Hand-authored, not fetched: this is a static, rarely-changing list with no upstream machine-readable classifier->SPDX mapping to pull from. Some classifiers are genuinely ambiguous between multiple real SPDX ids that share the SAME category (e.g. 'BSD License' doesn't distinguish BSD-2-Clause from BSD-3-Clause; 'Apache Software License' doesn't distinguish 1.1 from 2.0; 'Artistic License', 'Zope Public License', 'Eiffel Forum License', 'GNU Free Documentation License (FDL)', 'GNU General Public License (GPL)', and 'GNU Library or Lesser General Public License (LGPL)' all have the same shape of problem) - each is mapped to the single most common/current representative id, and category-based conflict logic is unaffected by the ambiguity since the plausible candidates share a category. Deliberately NOT mapped, by design, not oversight: the bare 'License :: OSI Approved' classifier (no specific license named); 'License :: OSI Approved :: Jabber Open Source License' and 'License :: OSI Approved :: MITRE Collaborative Virtual Workspace License (CVW)' (both real, rare OSI-approved classifiers with no corresponding id in our vendored spdx-licenses.json - rather than guess an id and risk corrupting the vendored SPDX set, these are left unmapped so resolution falls through to the next signal, e.g. license-file fingerprinting); 'License :: Public Domain' and 'License :: Freely Distributable' (no single SPDX id accurately represents these - mapping either to Unlicense or CC0-1.0 would overclaim a specific legal instrument that was never actually declared); and 'License :: Other/Proprietary License' (proprietary is definitionally not an SPDX license id). An unmapped classifier is not an error - mapClassifierToSpdxId returns undefined and the PyPI resolution pipeline (Milestone 4 Task 6) falls through to its next resolution step.",
